---
title: Risotto alla milanese
servings: 4
tags: [italian, vegetarian, gluten-free]
cuisine: italian
time: 45 minutes
source: Adapted from Risotto in cooklang/cookcli (MIT), https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cooklang/cookcli/main/seed/Risotto.cook
---

Bring the @vegetable stock{1%l} to a gentle simmer in a #saucepan{} and keep it
there. Steep the @saffron{1%pinch}(threads) in @water{2%tbsp}(warm).

Melt the @unsalted butter{30%g} in a #large heavy-bottomed pan{} and soften the
@yellow onion{1}(finely diced) ~{5%minutes} without colouring it.

Add the @arborio rice{320%g} and stir ~{2%minutes} to toast it. Pour in the
@dry white wine{100%ml} and let it cook away.

Add the hot stock a ladle at a time, stirring often and letting each ladle soak
in before the next, ~{18%minutes}, until the rice is tender with a little bite.

Off the heat, stir in the saffron water, the @parmesan{60%g}(grated) and
@unsalted butter{20%g}(cold, cubed) until creamy. Season with @salt{1%tsp} and
@black pepper{}. Rest ~{2%minutes} and serve on warm plates.

> Stock in slowly is the whole method; hurry it and the rice cooks unevenly.
